  "tagline": "Lightweight single-binary full-text search engine in Go with Elasticsearch-compatible ingest.",
  "description": "ZincSearch is a small Go search engine built on the bluge indexing library, created by the team that later built OpenObserve. It ships as one binary with an embedded web UI, accepts data through Elasticsearch-compatible bulk and index APIs, and needs a fraction of Elasticsearch's memory. The original company now steers log users to OpenObserve, and ZincSearch has become community-maintained; after a quiet 2024-25 it resumed releases in September 2026 with 0.4.11 and a 1.0 beta. Good for small app search or replacing a tiny Elasticsearch node, not for serious scale.",
